 succeeded in 0ms:
     1	# SF2 — one release gate
     2	
     3	17 October 2026. C2-B01/M01/M02/N01/N02 are repaired in this checkout. The shared policy is `sf2-release-v1`, bound to digest `6d47414ccaec24b199727771a301c93802f28115be72120f3cb461505cea9976`. This is a release-safety repair for experimental pseudo-labels, not independent print-truth qualification or approval to use a production L1 release.
     4	
     5	The observed checkout was `opus/spellcheck` at `c8b4974b07d001199a93a71ed24654e8c56fa954`: relative to the requested `2ac34b23`, that existing commit adds only the SF2 brief. No Git metadata was written. Other worktrees were read only. Network, CTC/R1 forward passes, GPU work, training and detector-geometry changes: **zero**. Detector execution was limited to the requested 92-line owner page and its detector control; M2 and L1r reused saved detector/R1 records. Evidence and source hashes are in [execution_receipt.json](SF2_evidence/execution_receipt.json).
     6	
     7	## C2-B01 — observation and uncertainty precede acceptance
     8	
     9	[`release_gate.py`](../../../greekocr/labelfix/release_gate.py) owns `decide`, `compose_reading`, `compose`, the serializer, the edit guard and the policy binding. M2's `combine` is its compatibility alias. Both the M2 measurement entry point and the current `agreement_mode.py` recompose saved runtime evidence through it. Combined owner pages call it directly; CN1 scores those hash-bound decisions. Both page builders use its serializer. Detector-only controls remain explicitly detector-only diagnostics.
    10	
    11	Per slot, the gate emits ACCEPT, KEEP (outside the R1 heads, with no proposed mark edit), or HOLD, with reasons. R1-target slots require a prediction and a scored coverage record. UNKNOWN, any recorded uncertainty, missing observation fields, malformed predictions, unresolved detector localisation/segmentation, unnamed marks, relevant clipping/UNSEEN zones, K1 flags and disagreement abstain. Duplicate coverage/prediction starts are rejected. PRESENCE compares named families; FULL compares named mark sets. Accepted names come from R1. A resolved fused sample remains eligible.
    12	
    13	With no validated observability masks, recorded top clipping is relevant to vowel/rho upper marks; bottom clipping is relevant to alpha/eta/omega subscripts, including a proposed absence. Existing left/right clipping or observation states are also consumed for preposed capital marks and word-final elisions. Irrelevant bottom clipping on rho does not itself veto a resolved slot. These are conservative release rules, not a claim that every coarse border flag identifies a truncated mark.
    14	
    15	The review's UNKNOWN/no-pixels, UNKNOWN/out-of-image, uncertain segmentation and relevant clipping correction witnesses now HOLD in both modes. Their previous result was unheld `ά → α`. Every L1r overlay, including unchanged and held lines, exports slot decisions, R1 coverage, detector uncertainty/clipping evidence, K1 flags and punctuation evidence. Old saved `modes` are never trusted by the release writer.
    16	
    17	## C2-M01 — supported edits and explicit punctuation policy
    18	
    19	The shared per-character guard permits mark edits only on matching Greek bases, using psili, dasia, acute, grave, circumflex, subscript and dialytika. It permits at most one mark per family, rejects incompatible breathing/dialytika and invalid bearer combinations, and applies K1 separately. Base substitutions are held. Unsupported Greek marks and non-Greek clusters must remain unchanged; their original raw spelling cannot be silently converted to NFC while another character is edited. An unchanged label retains its original bytes.
    20	
    21	The actual overlay witnesses `ᾱ → α`, `é → e`, and `ά̀ → α` change from **corrected → HOLD**, in both modes. Unsupported proposed marks are also rejected. M2's pair/control measurement applies this same guard to the original-label character before accepting an edit; recogniser inference remains reference-free.
    22	
    23	Punctuation is a separate detector policy: remove the recogniser's leading quote aliases and leading ASCII spaces, then emit canonical `“` exactly when opening-quote detector evidence exists. Compose canonical word-final `’` from the detector's elision decision. The release guard allows those word-final elision differences after Greek letters; it holds changes to other punctuation, internal/trailing whitespace or unsupported spacing-mark forms that cannot satisfy this correspondence. It does not strip arbitrary combining marks to compare skeletons. Edit offsets remain original-label NFD offsets; evidence offsets remain recogniser NFD offsets.
    24	
    25	## C2-M02 — identical composition, quotes and apostrophe custody
    26	
    27	The combined builder no longer skips absent R1 predictions or independently renders text. The two lost opening quotes on `384c3f89-p000030-l0010` and `...-l0029` are restored. Across all 92 owner lines, quote-glyph differences from the detector control are **5 → 0**; the old six rendered-text differences, including spacing, are removed. All **92/92** rebuilt page readings and per-slot states/reasons exactly match M2 recomposition of their saved detector evidence. All **15/15** previously unheld missing-prediction/localisation/unnamed witnesses now HOLD. See [owner_parity.json](SF2_evidence/owner_parity.json).
    28	
