I found two new gaps. SF3 uses the shorter capital side-mark zone for every capital, including Ι/Υ with diaeresis above the letter; a synthetic clipped `Ϊ → Ι` deletion is accepted. Also, runtime composition uses diagnostic E predictions when deciding whether bottom clipping matters, but the owner-page adapter omits them, so it can show ACCEPT where L1r holds. I’m saving reproducible witnesses and finishing the receipt checks.
